Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation (@mineralogy-and-petrology: 0, is #chapter, #mineralogy-and-petrology "foundations/Reading-minerals-and-rocks-from-zero.lingua#r_57NZD8HAVKQW409DEN9D771VK5") { r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN
Begin with a specimen or question about a material. Connect composition and structure with properties, learn to observe and analyze mineral/rock constituents, and explain how igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic, and related processes shaped the evidence. No prior specialist course is assumed; shared preparation appears where used.

[Read from a first specimen through substantial books and advanced studies](foundations/Reading-minerals-and-rocks-from-zero.lingua#r_57NZD8HAVKQW409DEN9D771VK5) starts with substantial book chapters and observations, growing through complete mineralogy/petrology books, English/Portuguese microscopy, full analytical methods, laboratories, university/graduate cases, quantitative phase and process models, and independent research. A reader can enter at a particular question and return for an unfamiliar foundation.

